From c0f4e1b5ffb709168050227f559b4030489c27f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:29:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(compression): rotation-mode history-refusal
 retry sends the current message once

Under the legacy compression.in_place: false, _adopt_grown_durable_parent adopted the
durable parent, which already holds the persisted current-turn row, and the caller's
verbatim_tail ([current]) was then rejoined onto it: the child session stored
"U\n\nU" and history_refusal_step appended current a third time to the retry request.

- The adoption drops the verbatim tail's durable copy from the adopted end (also covers
  /compress here N in rotation mode). The function moves to
  agent/conversation_compression_adopt.py to offset the FILE_LINES growth.
- history_refusal_step drops trailing user rows that only repeat the current text
  before appending it, and keys the one-retry cap on turn_id or _current_turn_id;
  without any turn identity it keeps the drop-and-notice path instead of looping.
- Tests: rotation-mode real-DB variant (request's last user content == current once,
  child session rows hold it once), folded-head and no-turn-id unit tests.

Follow-up of review t_01a1cef18e3ef70f (PR #1300).
